  "body": "## What changed\n\nSlice (a) of #1198 only: the viewport's five view buttons (Frame, Iso, Shaded/Wireframe, Toolpaths, World axes) move from the column under the view cube into a rounded, translucent grey ribbon resting on the bottom-left corner of the 3D pane. The cube stays top-right. The ribbon and its glyph painting live in the new `crates/ui/src/egui_app/viewport_bar.rs`; `viewcube.rs` shrinks from 459 to 313 lines. Button effects are unchanged (Frame queues `frame_all`, the toggles write view state as before).\n\nThe hud now needs room for the ribbon width (about 158 px), so panes between roughly 128 and 178 px wide lose the cube and buttons (previously kept). Decision recorded in `docs/decisions/1198-viewport-overlay-bar.md`.\n\nNo drag, move or rotate yet. Those are slices (b) to (d).\n\n## Slices remaining\n\n- (b) move handles with drag-to-move (one undoable transform command per drag, MCP tool needed)\n- (c) rotate\n- (d) snapping and typed values in the bar\n\n## How tested\n\nQuick gate `cargo xtask gate quick --base origin/main`: green on the first run. It ran the ui lib unit tests (which include `law_tests::the_hud_is_laid_out_from_the_pane_alone` and `viewport_bar::tests::bar_fits_its_buttons`) and the `boundary`, `boundary_picks` and `theme_files` suites. The egui_app click and nav tests are in the lib unit tests and use the new rects.\n\nPinning tests: `the_hud_is_laid_out_from_the_pane_alone` (ribbon centred, on the bottom edge, buttons inside it, no overlap with the cube, narrow-pane gate) and `bar_fits_its_buttons`.\n\n## What was not exercised\n\n- Nothing was looked at on screen. The ribbon colour and contrast on light and dark grounds are unverified.\n- No snapshot PNG was changed.\n- The bottom-right control hint is not moved; the centred ribbon should clear it on normal widths, but that is not seen.\n\n## Notes\n\n- No new user-facing command in this slice, so no MCP tool is needed yet. The MCP tool belongs with slice (b), which adds the transform command.\n- Process: draft only, not marked ready, not merged.\n\nChangelog: Viewport view buttons (frame, iso, shaded/wireframe, toolpaths, axes) move into a rounded control bar at the bottom of the 3D view (#1198, PR)\n\nRefs #1198\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
